Someone suggested [Go's profiler][1] to explore the codebase. It makes sense, you could
figure out the slow parts of your code, but what about other parts. What about parts
that aren't slow yet relevant ? Since the profiler takes samples every fixed interval,
it is bound to miss the fast functions.





[1]: https://go.dev/blog/pprof
